HST Office: the classic menu bar can be shown and hidden from the View menu and the "≡" menu, and owns Alt+letter
and F10 while it is shown.

The Tabbed UI hides the classic menu bar ("Thanh trình đơn"). It could be shown from the ribbon's View tab, but the
classic View menu had no item to hide it again, and the feature search (Alt+Q), which indexes the menu bar, did not
find the toggle. .uno:Menubar is now in the View menu of Writer, Calc and Impress, after Giao diện người dùng, and in
the "≡" menu at the right end of the tab row. In a mode without a ribbon the command is hidden and does nothing:
there the menu bar is the only way to the commands.

The "≡" menu loses Mới, Gần đây and Đóng (the File tab has them) and the user-interface and toolbar choosers (the
View menu and the ribbon's View tab keep them), as the project owner decided on 2026-11-13.

KeyTips (hst-ribbon-keytips.patch) took every Alt+letter that matches a tab, even when the menu bar was shown, so
its mnemonics did not work. With the menu bar shown, Alt+letter and F10 now go on to it (VCL and GTK open its
menus); Alt pressed and released alone still shows the ribbon tips. With the menu bar hidden, F10 shows the tips
as Alt does, and closes them again.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

